<main>
<section class="view" id="home"><div class="hero"><div class="hero-inner"><div class="eyebrow">A one-day gathering for creative minds</div><h1>Ideas are better<br>in motion.</h1><p>Join designers, founders, makers, and curious people for a day of honest conversations, practical workshops, and fresh ways to think about what comes next.</p><div class="hero-meta"><div><span>WHEN</span><b>Saturday · October 16, 2027</b></div><div><span>WHERE</span><b>Foundry Hall · Bengaluru</b></div><div><span>WHO</span><b>Creatives & curious builders</b></div></div><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="#register">Save your seat</a><a class="btn outline" href="#schedule">Explore the schedule</a></div></div></div><div class="wrap"><div class="row"><div><div class="eyebrow">A day to learn, question, and connect</div><h2 class="title">Not another conference.</h2></div></div><div class="grid"><article class="card"><span class="chip">OPEN IDEAS</span><h3>Real stories</h3><p class="sub">Honest lessons from the messy middle—not only the polished final result.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="chip">PRACTICAL TOOLS</span><h3>Useful workshops</h3><p class="sub">Take home ways of working you can put into practice on Monday.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="chip">GOOD COMPANY</span><h3>Room to connect</h3><p class="sub">Meet people from across design, culture, technology, and entrepreneurship.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="view" id="speakers"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">People with something worth sharing</div><h1 class="title">Meet the speakers.</h1><p class="sub">A generous mix of perspectives on making, working together, and imagining what comes next. Speaker profiles and links are illustrative for this event demo.</p><div class="grid"><article class="card speaker"><div class="speaker-img" role="img" aria-label="Speaker portrait placeholder"></div><div class="speaker-copy"><div class="eyebrow">Opening keynote · 10:00</div><h3>Priya Kapoor</h3><p class="meta">Designer & co-founder, Common Ground Studio</p><p class="sub">On building products that make room for more people.</p><a class="chip" href="https://www.linkedin.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Speaker profile ↗</a></div></article><article class="card speaker"><div class="speaker-img" role="img" aria-label="Speaker portrait placeholder"></div><div class="speaker-copy"><div class="eyebrow">Workshop · 11:30</div><h3>Jordan Lee</h3><p class="meta">Creative technologist & educator</p><p class="sub">A hands-on session about prototyping the questions that matter.</p><a class="chip" href="https://www.linkedin.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Speaker profile ↗</a></div></article><article class="card speaker"><div class="speaker-img" role="img" aria-label="Speaker portrait placeholder"></div><div class="speaker-copy"><div class="eyebrow">Closing conversation · 16:00</div><h3>Amara Nwosu</h3><p class="meta">Artist, author & community organizer</p><p class="sub">A conversation about sustainable creative practice and collective care.</p><a class="chip" href="https://www.linkedin.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Speaker profile ↗</a></div></article></div></div></section>
<section class="view" id="schedule"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Saturday · October 17 · Foundry Hall</div><h1 class="title">A day with room to think.</h1><div class="two"><div class="panel"><h2>Main stage</h2><div class="agenda"><div class="session"><time>09:00 — 09:45</time><h3>Doors, coffee & hello</h3><div class="meta">Arrival, introductions, and coffee with the community.</div></div><div class="session"><time>10:00 — 11:00</time><h3>Build for the edges, design for everyone</h3><div class="meta">Opening keynote with Priya Kapoor.</div></div><div class="session"><time>11:00 — 11:30</time><h3>A generous break</h3><div class="meta">Coffee, conversation, and the hallway track.</div></div><div class="session"><time>14:00 — 15:00</time><h3>Small experiments, meaningful change</h3><div class="meta">Stories from teams learning as they go.</div></div><div class="session"><time>16:00 — 17:00</time><h3>Making room to make</h3><div class="meta">Closing conversation with Amara Nwosu.</div></div></div></div><div class="panel"><h2>Workshops & gathering</h2><div class="agenda"><div class="session"><time>11:30 — 12:30</time><h3>Prototype the question</h3><div class="meta">Interactive workshop with Jordan Lee.</div></div><div class="session"><time>12:30 — 13:30</time><h3>Lunch together</h3><div class="meta">Vegetarian options and time to meet fellow attendees.</div></div><div class="session"><time>13:30 — 14:00</time><h3>Show & tell: works in progress</h3><div class="meta">A relaxed open-mic for works in progress.</div></div><div class="session"><time>17:00 onwards</time><h3>Closing reception</h3><div class="meta">An unhurried end to the day at Foundry Hall.</div></div></div><a class="btn" href="#register">Register to attend</a></div></div></div></section>
<section class="view" id="venue"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">A place to gather</div><h1 class="title">Foundry Hall, Bengaluru.</h1><div class="two"><div class="panel"><h2>Event details</h2><p><b>Saturday, October 16, 2027</b><br>9:00 am — 6:00 pm IST</p><p><b>Foundry Hall</b><br>12 Residency Road<br>Bengaluru, Karnataka 560025</p><p class="sub">The venue is centrally located near public transport. We encourage guests to check current local transit and accessibility details before traveling.</p><a class="btn outline" target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://maps.google.com/?q=Residency+Road+Bengaluru">Open venue map ↗</a></div><div class="panel"><div class="eyebrow">Who should join?</div><h2>For people who care about what they make.</h2><p class="sub">Creative Futures is for designers, independent makers, product teams, students, founders, community builders, and anyone curious about better ways to bring ideas into the world.</p><p class="sub">Come to learn from people outside your usual circle, find collaborators, and leave with a fresh perspective.</p><div class="notice">Demo event information: confirm actual venue, timings, prices, accessibility, and travel details with the organizer before attending.</div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="view" id="register"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Be part of the conversation</div><h1 class="title">Save your seat.</h1><div class="two"><div class="panel"><h2>Creative Futures Summit</h2><p>Saturday, October 16, 2027 · Foundry Hall, Bengaluru</p><p class="sub">A one-day gathering for creatives and curious builders. Choose a ticket type and we'll prepare a local demo confirmation.</p><p><span class="chip">General · ₹1,499</span> <span class="chip">Student · ₹799</span> <span class="chip">Community · Free demo ticket</span></p><p class="meta">Demo registration only; no payment is collected and no attendee details are sent to a server.</p></div><form id="registerForm" class="registration"><h2>Attendee registration</h2><label>Full name<input class="field" name="name" required autocomplete="name"></label><label>Email address<input class="field" name="email" type="email" required autocomplete="email"></label><label>Organization / school<input class="field" name="organization"></label><label>What best describes you?<select class="field" name="role"><option>Designer / maker</option><option>Student</option><option>Founder / entrepreneur</option><option>Technology professional</option><option>Community builder</option><option>Other</option></select></label><label>Ticket type<select class="field" name="ticket"><option value="General · ₹1,499">General · ₹1,499</option><option value="Student · ₹799">Student · ₹799</option><option value="Community · free demo ticket">Community · free demo ticket</option></select></label><label><input type="checkbox" required> I agree to the event code of conduct.</label><button>Complete demo registration</button><p id="registerStatus" class="status" role="status"></p><div id="ticket" class="ticket" hidden></div></form></div><div class="panel" style="margin-top:20px"><h2>Questions?</h2><p class="sub">For event inquiries, access needs, or group registrations, reach the organizing team.</p><a href="mailto:hello@creativefut